Z||000018||Nick||08-31-99||07:27 AM||||88 Fiero:<p>So basically, you had a modified car, and he had a car that looked like it should/would be modified but probably wasn't.  The big exhaust tip and tach don't mean shit.  They were probably just for looks.  Those punks are the ones that give imports a bad name.<p>My point was this.  If you had a stock Fiero, and were up against a stock CRX Si, both driven by professional drivers, it would be a very close race.  That's all.  I don't know how fast your car is, and I have no idea what that punk had in his car, and neither do you for that matter.  So to say that it doesn't matter if he is a good driver or not, and that the car just sucks is just plain ignorant or your part.  His car may have looked stupid and had mods that gave no performance gain, but it doesn't change what the car is underneath all that.  <p>I will agree with the statement made by LowCG that front wheel drive cars are not as much fun to drive as a Fiero, or any rear driven car for that matter. <p>DXR_WILL:  The Integra GS-R is the faster of that bunch.  But yes, all 3 will give the Fiero a good race, provided they aren't driven by some racer-wannabe punk who can't shift correctly.
Z||000019||88 Fiero||08-31-99||09:11 AM||||Nick...I apologize if I offend you with those remarks...reason I said that this CRX sucks!!! because one it's 1.6 liter second the first generation of CRX is not a winner and anybody can agree to that...second the is not even wider...it's taller than the rood of a fiero..so I know right off that when he and I race...he is not going to win it not matter what's the situation. third things on my car would not really considered modified. been involve with the fiero since '85 and belong to the FOCOA Club here in California. Keith Huff is a long time and very good friend and been involve every aspect of the car...I've been to the Fiero Factory too and seen the tooling that was use on this car...it doesn't matter to me what you drive or anybody drives...but getting sick and tired of hearing that fiero's are piece of junk which is not true!!! there are alot of potential with this car including engine conversions and bodykits which you don't see in any production car...and if you really think that the CRX is a hot car then what are doing driving a fiero...there's got to be a good reason for that and don't tell because you just like it co'z it's a lame excuse....I have to import cars that I drive everyday plus my '88 GT and will never touch this import cars for performance co'z to me it's not worth it...
Z||000020||Nick||08-31-99||10:56 AM||||No, you didn't offend me.  I love the Fiero just as much as you guys do.  I hated having to sell mine, but it was a financial thing.  But you seem to doubt the potential of the 1.6L 4-banger, and you seem to think that the ride height/width of the CRX makes it inferior in a race.  Well, I'm not going to get into that, so if you want to discuss it, email me.  :-) <p>I didn't realize you were talking about a first gen. CRX.  I agree that those are not only ugly, but slow too.  Mine is a second gen.(88-91) CRX Si, and the performance numbers according to MotorTrend were similar to those of my 86 GT fastback 5-speed, in both acceleration and slalom.  So that was my only point.  I like both cars, but for entirely different reasons.  They are just too different for us to be getting into a pissing contest about which one is better or faster.  In the end it all comes down to personal tastes and opinions anyways.  So I won't try to change your mind if you don't try to change mine.  Deal?<p>I agree with you about being sick of people trying to say that all Fieros are junk.  I've had to deal with that with both my Fiero and my Honda.  So I understand your frustration.<p>
Z||000021||CUTTER||08-31-99||02:07 PM||||Yeah, people always call my 87GT a deathtrap and say it will catch on fire when I am driving down the street. But I tell them to go suck a ......nevermind. then when I race them and beat the hell outa them....then I dont hear them talking any bull. They finally realize the fiero...king of american mid-engine sports cars(because they are the only american made mid-engine sports car)is a very nice, fast car. Hey what can I say??? Fieros RULE!!!!!
Z||000022||DJRice||09-01-99||07:11 AM||||First, let me say that I do not drive any foreign cars.  I, like everybody else here, do enjoy my Fiero immensley.  But I just read an artilcle in the new Car & Driver last night that im going to mention to throw gas on this fire.<p>Honda has just developed an engine for their S2000 that is a 4-banger with a displacement of about 120 cubic inches.  This engine develops 240 hp, or 2 hp per c.i. (still gets 30mpg) I only mention this because technology has moved to the point that smaller engines can develop alot of horsepower, at the price of torque. Any engine you can wind above 8000rpm is bound to move a small car pretty fast. <p>Dont get me wrong, I doubt that this car is half as fun to drive as our Fiero's are. In fact, I think that youd have to look long and hard to find a car with as much character as the Fiero does.  <p>American car makers decided to ignore technology for a while and adopt the "If it aint broke dont fix it" attitude.  The development of the Fiero changed that a little bit, but Pontiac Scrapped it.  Several years later, GM took what it learned from Fiero and developed Saturn.<p>Ford has just recently started to change a bit with the 4.6L DOHC 4 Valve per cylinder V8 in the Mustangs that develop almost as much HP as a GM 5.7L.<p>The Japanese dont have that attitude.  They know that if they build the piston right, build the block right, make sure it is cooled and lubed properly, they can build a small engine that will rev high and develop some big horsepower. Throw a Turbo Charger on it and BAM! You have a fast little car with less engine displacment then the average Coca-Cola<br>jug.<p>My point was this, with enough money and technology invested, you can build a 4 cyl that will outrun a 6 or even 8 cyl.  No one needs to take offense at that, its a fact.
Z||000023||DJRice||09-01-99||07:13 AM||||Jeez, I didnt realize I had been typing that long.....That was quite a sermon.
Z||000024||four50four||09-01-99||04:24 PM||||yeah, but with enough money you can make a v6 faster than ANY 4 cylinder, and in turn, you can make a v8 faster than ANY v6, and in turn, you can make a v10 faster than ANY v8, and in turn, you can make a v12 faster than ANY v10, well, you get the point.
